{
  "id": "Compound::DB00196 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "Fluconazole is implicated in the regulation of Cyp2c9 through a complex network of interactions involving cytochrome P450 enzymes. The evidence suggests that Fluconazole, as a member of the Cytochrome P450 2c19 inhibitors, indirectly influences Cyp2c9 via its interaction with other compounds like Omeprazole and Efavirenz. These compounds, in turn, bind to Cyp2c9, indicating a direct regulatory role. The shared involvement of Fluconazole and these inhibitors in the same pathway highlights a potential mechanism where Fluconazole may modulate Cyp2c9 activity through the inhibition of its enzymatic function. The presence of an oxygen molecular entity as a common ancestor further suggests a broader metabolic pathway that connects Fluconazole to Cyp2c9, reinforcing the idea of a metabolic interaction. This integrated evidence points to a possible role of Fluconazole in modulating Cyp2c9 activity, likely through the inhibition of its enzymatic function, thereby influencing the metabolism of other substrates.",
